    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d571">

                <pb facs="0741" n="455" xml:id="pg455"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/10209</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-10T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 10, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3913. Department’s 3872.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d571-f1"/> Consul, Trinidad,
                    telegraphs American S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Pathfinder</hi> delayed there
                    at cost $1,500 daily while awaiting permit from London for bunker coal. Bring
                    matter to attention Foreign Office in connection with similar cases and inquire
                    if it is established practice of British Government to accord to American
                    vessels treatment this character which has in several instances resulted in
                    serious loss to vessels. Request prompt reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
